    {
      "id": 9140,
      "name": "Posco",
      "username": "Posco",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/f19dbf/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-12-17T18:49:08.000Z",
      "cooked": "<div>We played our first game yesterday and I've been trying some more to sort out the timing questions that arose</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Looking at the FAQ I believe there are definitely two principles</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>1) simultaneous effects are actually resolved in order (of the players choosing)</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>2) If an effect is triggered, it is fully resolved before continuing with those simultaneous effects (and can affect/amend/cancel those effects)</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>so are the following correct</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>a card effect attacks all hero targets</div><div>The players select the first hero target</div><div>By selecting that hero target, an effect/power destroys the card causing the attack</div><div>all the remaining attacks are cancelled</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>a card effect attacks all hero targets for 2 damage and another card gives a bonus 1 to the attack for a total of 3 damage</div><div>The players select the first hero target</div><div>By selecting that hero target, an effect/power destroys the card causing the bonus 1</div><div>all the remaining attacks are value 2 (even though \"simultaneous\")</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>However, my main concern (because the other players didn't feel it was correct) is the following</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Unity's&nbsp;Cryo Bot receives damage that would destroy it</div><div>However, when damage is dealt to it, it deals damage to non-hero targets</div><div>Does being destroyed, prevent the possible triggers on the card. (In our game we found this is important for Cryo Bot and Lady Luck)</div><div>I emailed Mike Booth (Spiffworld) and he seemed to think that being destroyed would prevent the triggers but it didn't sit well with the group yesterday.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>(we were playing with more complex characters as I had received Shattered Timelines and the mini-expansions but the base game has failed to arrive as yet ! &nbsp;However, the questions remain valid for us)</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Thanks</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Ian</div>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:39:51.275Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
