      "id": 84551,
      "name": "Foote",
      "username": "Foote",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-12-17T19:24:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>This is all correct it seems so far.</p><p>Allow me just pose a quick senario to demonstrate that simultaneous triggers and consecutive triggers can be different, just to cover all the bases here.</p><p>Villain plays imaginary card [V1] which reads: \"Play the top card of the Villain deck. Then, destroy all hero ongoing cards\". The next Villain card in the deck is the imaginary card [V2] which reads: \"Destroy all Villain cards in play\".&nbsp;</p><p>In this senario, all three of these effects are consecutive triggers. Consecutive triggers, unlike simultaneous triggers, resolve in order of newest to oldest. You would have to resolve the card [V2] before you moved on to the second effect clause of [V1]. End result would be that the heros would not have their ongoings destroyed.</p><p>Edit: Also, going to be nitpicky, its \"Cryo\" bot, not Gyro. Cryo = greek for \"icey cold\".&nbsp;</p>",
